@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+---
+id: task-001-give-each-task-a-stable-id
+type: task
+title: "Give each task a stable id"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Give each task a unique id, stable across a rename, so the app has a way to refer to a task that
+survives a title change.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `Task` (`src/domain/task.ts`) gained a required `id: string` field; `createTask` now takes the id as a
+  parameter instead of inventing one, to stay clock- and randomness-free per `r3-no-clock-or-randomness`.
+- `TaskList` (`src/domain/list.ts`) gained a `get(id)` method. `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`,
+  `tag`, `untag` and `remove` now accept either a task's title or its id.
+- The list assigns ids from a private, monotonically increasing counter (`t1`, `t2`, ...), never reused,
+  and is now keyed internally by id rather than by title.
+- Tests added to `test/list.test.ts`: id uniqueness and stability across rename, `get` on an unknown id,
+  every title-taking method accepting an id, and ids not being reused after a remove. Written and
+  confirmed failing before the implementation (red, then green).
+
+See decision-log `dl-001-stable-task-ids-via-a-per-list-sequential-counter` for the design rationale.
+
+## Verification
+
+`npm test`: 10/10 passing.
